MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_001: Hold, Lilian. Just where are you off to?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_002: Uh...into town.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_003: Then you won't mind if I join you. Or will you?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_004: Suit yourself, but I'm just going shopping to restock\nsome stuff.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_005: Don't tell me you play bodyguard for every soldier\nwho leaves the grounds.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_006: Or are you keeping an eye on me to make sure I don't\nskip out on my duties?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_007: That is it exactly. I cannot rule out the possibility of\nyou meeting with assassins from Dyan's faction.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_008: No minced words here, huh? At least you're up-\nfront about it.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_009: But you really think I'm some traitor who's wormed\nher way in here?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_010: Between your insolence to Her Majesty and your\npersonal history, I cannot help but be suspicious.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_011: You give me way too much credit. I don't have the\nskills or the guts for that.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_012: My house may have sided with Prince Dyan,\nbut I'm not here to pull anything.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_013: So you say. But a truly capable warrior masks\ntheir intent.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_014: It is my duty to prevent anything from threatening\nHer Majesty's safety.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_015: So I hope you don't have any outrageous plans of\nrestoring the Dyan faction.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_016: I told you that's not what I'm about. Quit worrying.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_017: I'm here to get paid, and that's it. I'd be an idiot to\nbite the hand that feeds me.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_018: I fail to see how your willingness to do anything for\na price is meant to comfort me.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_019: Oh, I was a fool to expect loyalty from one motivated\nby greed.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_020: Oh, don't worry—I'm learning a lot about you too.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_021: I gotta get going. This shopping isn't gonna do itself.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_022: Wait! I am not done talking to— Ugh...
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_023: Her house sided with Dyan, and she's interested\nsolely in gold.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_C_024: I am more concerned than ever that assassins might\nhire her. Who can predict those without loyalties?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_001: Lilian, I've heard the recent reports.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_002: The cover you provided saved the lives of our front\nline. I thank you on behalf of Her Majesty.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_003: Yeah, no problem. Listen, my shift's over, so I'm\ngonna head back to my room.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_004: And I'll want a bonus for saving those troops.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_005: {SetColor=Gray}The money issue again...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_006: Wait, Lilian. I have a question.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_007: Yeah? Am I gonna get paid to answer it?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_008: Let us say I offered you an exorbitant sum never to\ncontact anyone from Dyan's faction again.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_009: What would you say to that?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_010: Easy. I'd say no.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_011: Oh? And why is that? I see no downside in it for you.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_012: If you are truly loyal to Her Majesty, it would be\na hefty payment for doing nothing.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_013: Yeah, but under those terms, I couldn't get in touch\nwith my parents either.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_014: My whole thing is trying to buy back our estate so\nmy family can live like we used to.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_015: The money's useless if I gotta cut contact with my\nfolks. So, no, thanks.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_016: That's it? You care nothing of Dyan or your house's\nstatus? Only a return to your old life?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_017: Eh...
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_018: Hm. I thought your greed was simple, but I see now\nthere is a nobler aspect to it.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_019: Huh. You believe me?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_020: If you were truly money hungry, you should have\nleapt at my request to betray Dyan's faction.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_021: But you did not. You have no loyalty to Prince\nDyan—only love for your family.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_022: Therefore my scheme to ferret out your intentions\nwas based on false premises. Hohoho.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_023: Whatever. I answered your question, right?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_024: Are you gonna kick loose a bonus for that? I'll take\nwhatever you're offering.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_025: You are incorrigible. No, you are not getting paid for\nanswering a simple question. Run along, now.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_026: Tsk. Figures.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_027: However, I will speak to Her Majesty about an\nincrease to your wages.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_B_028: Appreciate it. Fingers crossed for you!
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_001: Who have we here? Ah, Lilian.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_002: Hey, Bonaventure. Still got your eye on me?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_003: I talked some stuff out with Queen Theodora, so\nthere's probably no need.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_004: Indeed there is not.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_005: As Her Majesty has given her approval, it is not\nmy place to undermine her judgment.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_006: Seems like you're letting it go easily for a guy who's\nbeen watching me like a hawk.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_007: As to that, I concluded on my own that you are\ntrustworthy.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_008: You did? Oh. Uh. I don't have a comeback for that.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_009: In a fair assessment, you are both skilled with a bow\nand mindful of your comrades-in-arms.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_010: You are guided by a fondness for your parents and\na desire to buy back your happiest days with them.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_011: So you are unlikely to resort to treachery. It would\nreflect poorly on them for only a bit of coin.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_012: Yeah, pretty much. You finally get me, huh?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_013: I feel like I understand where you're coming from\nwith the whole loyalty thing too.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_014: My chat with Queen Theodora showed me that\nHer Majesty is the real deal.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_015: I'm sure my dad had his reasons to take Prince\nDyan's side.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_016: And someday, he and I are going to have a talk\nabout that.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_017: A sound idea. Even blood relatives can have stark\ndifferences of opinion.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_018: But I cannot see yours developing into rifts. Not with\nthe love you bear for your family.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_019: Thanks, Bonaventure.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_020: Hm! Your parents must be proud to have such a\ndevoted daughter.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_021: What, are you jealous? No kids of your own,\nso they say.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_022: You could always hire me for appearances.\nHugs extra.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_023: That is absurd. What would your parents say if\nthey heard you now? Honestly!
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_024: Oh, wait—or is it a fake wife you're looking for?
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_025: Hmm, I'm not sure people would buy that one.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_026: If you're going to joke around, at least don't undercut\nthe punch line.
MID_SE_Bon_Lil_A_027: Hahaha! Hey, who says I was joking? Eh?